WEBVTT

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:02.950
<i>It's a missile!</i>

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.880
<i>This isn't a Scooper missile!</i>

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:05.940
What is it, then?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.650
It's an International Defense Force bomb!

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.150
At this rate, we'll all die!

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.480
This is serious!

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.700
<i>I want to protect the city.</i>

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.380
<i>I want to stay here.</i>

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.600
<i>This place is everything to me.</i>

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.880
Their self-defense system has activated!

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.580
Is that...

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.440
It's the parfait we were talking about!

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.860
It looks delicious!

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.890
Yeah, it does look delicious.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.440
But this is no time to eat!

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.450
Such creativity!

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.240
It's incredible!

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.240
What is this wall?

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.540
It's the surface of a sphere.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.610
It's like a giant sphere 
is surrounding the area.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:55.440
Yeah!

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.940
As though all of Harajuku has 
been enveloped by a big bubble!

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.200
A bubble?

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.690
In other words...

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.830
In other words, it's a giant bubble.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.160
A Harajuku bubble!

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:07.490
A bubble?

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.460
It looked to me like this wall 
came from that parfait.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.250
Wow, really?

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.990
But how does that work?

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.930
Hold on. I'll analyze it.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:21.310
But I don't know where to start looking!

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.710
I've never experienced anything like this!

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.770
Yeah, it's a new experience.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.170
I would've preferred to avoid this one.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:37.250
But without this bubble you created 
using the power of the Amatsumara,

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:46.110
we would've been killed by the Scoopers' 
attack or by the IDF's bomb.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.560
The fact that we're still alive is 
the silver lining in this situation.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.690
Maybe so, but the IDF still 
dropped a bomb on us.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.940
Does that mean that the
 adults have abandoned us?

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:59.850
I guess so.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:03.340
But you three protected us, indeed!

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.300
I'm Rito.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.540
I'm Kotoko.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.180
And this is Mari-chan.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.930
Am I the only one having a 
hard time accepting this?

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:14.810
What are we supposed to do now?

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.520
Don't tell me we have to live 
inside this thing forever.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:27.530
I believe this bubble appeared in response 
to your desire to protect Harajuku.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.240
So isn't this what you wanted?

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.180
You're exactly right.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:38.260
Being attacked by mysterious 
aliens, trapped inside a bubble,

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:42.280
and not knowing what happens next 
sounds like a wonderful weekend!

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.300
Just unimaginably wonderful!

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.080
Kotoko, stay with Mari.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:47.860
Huh?

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:51.960
Mari only gets like that when she's scared.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:55.100
You're right. Got it!

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.630
Mari-chan!

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:57.440
What?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.780
Mari-chan, I'll stick by you the whole time.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:02.180
We'll be together all day today,
both asleep and awake.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:06.160
Didn't you say before that you wished 
we could live in Harajuku together?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.040
Yeah, I did.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.330
This isn't at all like 
what I imagined, though.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.320
Rito-chan, wait!

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:19.880
We don't know what that wall is made of.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.550
It might be better not to touch it.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.220
You're right.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.570
It's okay as long as I don't touch it, right?

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:34.980
Y-Yeah, I guess.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:40.320
Judging by that sound, 
this wall seems pretty hard.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.260
It certainly seems that way.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.440
I don't have service!

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.410
This wall is blocking the signal.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.060
Huh?

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.140
You're right.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:52.850
Does that mean we can't make 
calls or send e-mails, either?

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.410
In this day and age?

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.450
I know!

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:59.060
My parents told me I'm on my 
phone and tablet too much,

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:00.840
so this may have been good timing!

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.010
Seriously.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.900
No, wait. It's not good at all.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.800
This means I can't call my family.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:14.440
I wonder if this wall will prevent 
my grandma from coming home.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.770
This means we can't leave either, right?

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:22.450
Mari, we should be grateful the 
three of us are still together.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:22.980
Right?

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.690
Yeah. Sorry.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:27.840
It's okay, Mari.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.550
I'm scared, too. I don't know what to do.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:33.860
But having you and Kotoko 
here is keeping me sane.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.590
I agree.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:39.070
You're such good friends, indeed.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.250
Such wonderful friendship!

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.520
That's another thing the Scoopers lack.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.900
I won't deny our friendship.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:51.640
Hey, I'm not detecting 
any energy in this wall.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.260
Its composition seems 
similar to that of glass.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.830
It's really hard, though.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.810
So it's like frosted glass 
that lets light through?

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.080
I think so.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:01.810
If it's glass...

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.040
Wait, Rito, what are you doing?

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.460
I thought I'd try cutting it.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.660
It's not working.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.000
It's really hard.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.560
But there's a slight scratch on the wall.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:27.300
See?

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.470
It fixed itself!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.760
This isn't just magic. It's a miracle.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:37.370
It seems to be capable of self-repair.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.940
Is it alive?

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:42.060
I don't understand. My brain isn't working.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:45.150
I wish I had time to organize my thoughts.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.730
It's okay. You don't have to think.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:50.050
The gears in Kotoko's brain are 
probably turning as fast as they can.

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:51.750
Let's examine what's underground.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:55.400
I want to try searching for a way 
out of this bubble from all angles!

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.150
See?

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:58.360
I'm glad she seems to be having fun.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.050
It's pitch black.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.900
The power isn't even on.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.440
This place is scary.

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:15.720
Stay by me.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.310
I have no intention of letting go of your arm.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:21.080
If you're scared, you can wait here.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.390
The two of us can go. Right, Rito-chan?

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:24.460
Yeah.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.980
Misa-chan, are you going to wait here, too?

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:30.940
I'd like to stay with all of you, indeed.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.820
And I shall accompany you, as well.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.950
Watch your step.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:42.000
It's really dark.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:50.590
This is...

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.160
It's blocked underground, too.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.420
Too bad.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.660
At least we know now.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.470
So can we head back to the surface?

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.050
I can't stand this darkness.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:02.720
What? What? What?

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.690
The power's on?

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.270
I don't know why, but lucky us!

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.230
Yeah, we're lucky, all right.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:12.990
I'm so happy, it's like my birthday 
and Christmas came at the same time.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:16.840
Looks like the power's back on in the city.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.700
Does the bubble allow electricity through?

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.270
That's convenient.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.180
But we're still trapped, right?

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.000
It seems that way.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.380
I'm still not used to being trapped in here!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.950
The inside of the bubble 
seems pretty spacious.

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:34.520
Its radius is 720 meters.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:44.600
I don't feel as trapped on the surface.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.560
We're still trapped, though.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:50.530
What's wrong?

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:51.610
Something's there!

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.630
It looked like an organism.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:54.320
Indeed.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.400
What kind of organism?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.580
Don't you even tell me it's an alien!

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.530
It was probably a cat.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:04.370
Oh! Like that cat you take care of!

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.880
Hey, you're right. It's that cat.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.890
A cat? Is that an organism endemic to Earth?

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:13.990
I'll go look for it.

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.550
Me, too.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:16.460
Wha...

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.680
Then I'm coming with you!

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:20.460
We'll all go together, indeed.

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:22.310
We shall join you.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.740
Kitty!

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:28.230
Where are you?

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:30.120
Hey...

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:33.190
Rito, you didn't name the cat?

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:36.260
No. It's not mine or anything.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.110
It's better off free.

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.230
Meow.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:45.940
It came!

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:46.880
Shh.

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:55.320
You like fish sausages, right?

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:07.500
It got scared.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.090
Maybe it saw me.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:14.980
Yeah, it's almost definitely your fault.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.860
If there's someone who wouldn't be afraid of 
a talking fried shrimp, I'd like to meet them.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:23.520
Kitty, don't you want some fish sausage?

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.940
It'll eat it if we leave it here.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:27.480
Let's head back to Park.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.300
Okay.

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:30.330
Right.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:46.740
I wonder why our parfait is 
hanging in the sky, though.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:47.630
Yeah.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.850
What's going to happen to us?

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.960
What about our meals, drinks, and snacks?

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.440
Mari-chan, that's what 
you're most worried about?

00:11:57.310 --> 00:12:01.020
If it comes to it, we could 
probably eat that parfait.

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:11.840
It's delicious, indeed.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.960
Is this what they call Japanese tea?

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:20.200
No, it's chamomile tea, so I 
guess that makes it foreign.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:22.760
It's said to be the oldest herb in the world.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.610
It's supposed to help you relax.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:29.730
I see you're familiar with 
a variety of cultures.

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:32.000
I'm exhausted.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.190
Today was like an unfunny B-movie.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:38.770
Mari, you like B-movies.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:42.470
Yeah, but I wouldn't want to be in one.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:49.020
I wish I could eat citron and pepper popcorn 
while watching <i>Gone with the Wind</i>.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:52.200
I know. We don't have popcorn, 
but we do have donuts.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:54.160
You mean...

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:00.800
Here!

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:05.110
I analyzed them, and they're 
just like regular donuts.

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:08.370
We should be able to eat them, 
and I suspect they're delicious.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.760
I'd believe you if you'd eaten one first.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.850
Yeah. It's good.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.310
Indeed.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.960
It really is delicious!

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.660
The combination of strong flour, 
weak flour, and dry yeast is perfect!

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.000
And the sweetness is refined sugar.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.730
You want me to eat it, right?

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:28.770
If you insist, I will.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.210
I'm surprised. It really is good.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.080
Isn't it?

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.880
Sweets are so strange.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.540
Eating them calms me down.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.130
Eating donuts here makes it 
feel like an ordinary afternoon,

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:46.380
but I wonder what's going 
on outside the bubble.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.970
Let's listen to the radio.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:55.300
<i>Yesterday, the Scoopers stole 
famous structures around Tokyo.</i>

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:53.600
It's DJ Aoyama!

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.430
Since this is being broadcast 
from a studio in Shinjuku,

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:57.210
<i>Their intentions are still unknown,</i>

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:58.140
we're receiving signals from outside.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:59.560
<i>and the government response 
is seesawing back and forth.</i>

00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.550
That's good.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:01.520
Everyone's safe outside the bubble, too.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.900
<i>The situation is extremely confusing.</i>

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:02.440
Yeah!

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:05.660
<i>Additionally, the mysterious 
dome that suddenly appeared</i>

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:09.730
<i>in my beloved Harajuku 
is being investigated.</i>

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:14.460
I guess the people outside don't know 
what's going on inside, either.

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:11.840
<i>What is that thing?</i>

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:14.470
<i>Mysterious, isn't it? What is it...</i>

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:17.180
Huh? Maybe there's interference.

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:18.930
What? What? What?

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:20.230
Is it the Scoopers again?

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:21.890
I think so.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:25.630
But can they break through the bubble?

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.190
It's dented.

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:39.230
I'm detecting powerful energy waves.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:44.070
They might be trying to 
punch a hole in the bubble.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:47.480
The Scoopers must be desperate, too.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:51.160
They're determined to steal Harajuku.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.170
We won't let them.

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:54.800
Yeah.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:55.990
We're fighting again?

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:57.750
We have to defend it.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:11.390
What's going on?

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:16.010
You shifted the inside of 
the bubble to hyperspace.

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:20.240
In other words, you created a barrier.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:23.900
You'll be able to defend Harajuku now.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.350
A barrier?

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:28.600
In other words, you've created

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.650
a hidden Harajuku—an Urahara.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.300
Urahara...

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:58.100
That's inconveniently large.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.890
I know! It must be the final boss!

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.540
I bet it's strong!

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:06.990
Most definitely. Girls, 
that is no ordinary Scooper.

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.280
Then what is it?

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:11.940
One who possesses great power 
even among the Scoopers themselves.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:16.660
Its fighting capabilities are likely 
magnitudes greater than the others'.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:20.360
It's here to steal all of 
Harajuku's cute things?

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:21.560
Precisely.

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:27.750
Its target is this neighborhood's culture 
and all the creative things you've built.

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:30.560
We have to stop it.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.640
Be careful, indeed.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:37.050
Misa-chan, go hide.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.660
Indeed.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:40.770
Let's go.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.310
Yeah.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.790
I'll analyze the big one.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.160
It's covered in bumps.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.490
I wonder what they are...

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.530
It's coming this way! It's getting closer!

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:01.620
I'll distract it.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:32.670
Rito-chan, you're going faster than 
it can keep up with. It's slow!

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:34.300
Mari, use your cannon.

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.070
I'll draw it within your range.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:38.960
Just so you know, I'm not at 
all confident I can hit it.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.260
It's okay.

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:42.790
It should automatically aim for you.

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.160
Go, Mari.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:49.040
Aw, jeez!

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.700
Mari-chan, fire!

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:57.130
Seriously, don't blame me if I miss!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:08.410
Huh?

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:09.560
It was deflected.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:23.520
Are you okay?

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:24.540
Do I look okay?

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:26.330
Don't be scared.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.500
We'll protect you.

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:40.890
My old friend.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.870
Huh? It's getting warmer.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:58.900
Kotoko, it's shooting at us from far away.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.840
Mari-chan, fire the cannon again!

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.960
I can't!

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:02.820
We'll do it together.

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:13.210
Mari, now.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:13.670
Okay!

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:28.240
<i>Before the big one spits out 
rocks, its body gets really hot.</i>

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:32.280
<i>I don't know why yet, but I expect that...</i>

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:34.120
Kotoko, what do we need to know?

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:38.740
I think the moment its body gets hot 
and it opens its mouth is your window.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:43.470
That moment is probably its weakness.

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:44.180
<i>That moment is probably its weakness.</i>

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:47.790
<i>I'll give you the signal when its body 
temperature reaches 180 degrees Celsius.</i>

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:48.920
Okay.

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:50.840
You want me to shoot, right?

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:52.760
I'm not confident I can hit it, though.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:59.670
It's getting warmer. Almost there...

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:07.130
Okay, it's within range.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.230
All right, it's 180 degrees!

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.180
Mari-chan, shoot!

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:15.560
Rito-chan's in danger!

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.520
You want me to shoot, right?

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:31.060
All right!

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.860
Yay! We got another prize!

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:51.880
This Scooper turned into popcorn!

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:53.240
How cute!

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:56.480
This is great. I was just craving popcorn, too.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.190
While watching <i>Gone with the Wind</i>, that is.

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.690
It smells like caramel.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:07.780
It tastes like caramel corn, too.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:09.890
You're eating again?

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:12.090
These are strawberry flavor.

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.860
The matcha flavor is good, too.

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:17.120
You want me to eat it, right?

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:19.880
Citron and pepper!

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:22.340
That's your favorite flavor.

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:26.190
Rito, thanks for earlier.

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:32.850
I was happy when you said you'd protect me.

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:37.780
Your sacrifice was not in vain.

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:29.090
Delicious! No wonder Harajuku 
is famous for its crêpes!

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:30.810
Misa-sama, it's an emergency!

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:33.760
Crêpes are an invasive type of cuisine!

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:34.970
What? Really?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:37.720
But they're delicious, 
so I don't care what they are.

00:23:37.720 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>illustrated by Tamano Hazuki</b>
